    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Do you often feel restless or like you have to move around when you’re supposed to sit still?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S012",
      "patient_response": "Yeah, definitely. Like, if I'm stuck on a long Zoom call for a lecture, or if I'm just supposed to be sitting quietly working on something, I start getting this weird, uncomfortable pressure in my body. It's like I just have to get up and pace around, or at least be doing something with my hands. Which reminds me, I actually bought this really cool fidget cube online last week. It has all these little buttons and switches on it, and it was supposed to be delivered yesterday, but the tracking app said there was a delay. I don't know why shipping is always so messed up lately. My roommate ordered a pair of shoes like three weeks ago and they still haven't shown up. She was so mad because she wanted to wear them to a party this weekend. But anyway, yeah, sitting still is super hard for me. I just feel like I need to be moving.",
