      "doctor_question": "Have you often gotten into trouble for being impulsive, defiant, or acting out toward teachers, parents, or other authority figures?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Um, no, not really. I mean, I'm not mean to teachers or anything. I don't really act out. Actually, I had this one professor last semester for Intro to Psych, Dr. Harrison, and he was super strict. Like, if you were even two minutes late, he'd literally lock the door. Which is so unfair because the lecture hall is in the basement of the science building, and the elevators there are incredibly slow. \n\nOne time, I got stuck in that elevator with this girl who had a pet iguana in her backpack. Like, a literal live iguana. She told me it was an emotional support animal, but I really don't think the school allows reptiles in the dorms. My RA told us during orientation we could only have fish. Which, honestly, fish are so boring. I had a betta fish in middle school named Barnaby and he just kind of floated there until he died. \n\nBut, um... wait, what were you asking? Oh, right, getting in trouble. Yeah, no, I'm usually pretty respectful to authority figures and stuff.",
